// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/fpga/sar_adc_ax7203.t27 -- the SAR converter of the golden deck on the ALINX AX7203: 31 conversions, one UART receipt line each
; M4e-board of the SAR ADC milestone (#10524, epic #10486, issue #10910). The converter is specs/analog/sar_adc.t27 (M4e, #10818): the M4a split
; capacitive DAC with its 1-unit bridge and one fitted top-plate parasitic (specs/analog/sar_cdac.t27), a sign comparator with one fitted offset,
; the MSB-first sequence of the deck, run on the 31 held samples of our own ngspice + PSP103 run. This file is the board top of it: the words
; of the DAC, the samples and the two pinned codes of each conversion are ROMs, and the machine below walks the spec's sequence on the fabric.
; The converter's functions (neg_word, decide, convert_sar, model_k, round_back, add_sm, pack, fold), M0's PLL, UART frame and verdict
; constants and the receipt's digits (specs/fpga/board_receipt.t27) come in by `use`; what is written here is the machine, the ROMs and the
; line of the receipt. Everything hand-written is this file. Nothing of M1b (specs/fpga/analog_cell_ax7203.t27) is edited; its pattern is
; followed: the restart request flags, the ROM as an if-chain, the receipt as segments, the tests that run the machine beside the spec.
; -
; THE CONVERSION (sar_adc.t27, sar_core). A conversion holds the two top plates at the sample, xp = V(VDP) and xn = V(VDN), as words (bit 31 =
; negative, bits 0..30 the magnitude in units of 2^-24 V). Decision i = 0 .. 10, MSB first: b = (xp - xn + OFF > 0); then, for i < 10, the plate of
; Bit_(10 - i) moves, down for the P half and up for the N half when b is set, the other way when it is clear, by rnd(K x VCM), K the plate's Vout
; ratio. The code is the eleven decisions. The spec runs net1 too; it never reaches the comparator and nothing reads it, so the board does not
; (a test runs both nodes of the spec beside the machine and compares Vout after every decision).
; -
; THE MACHINE, one step a clock at 100 MHz (the PLL of M0 from the 200 MHz oscillator), the same for every conversion:
;   P_SMP   xp and xn from the sample ROM, the two pinned codes from theirs
;   P_NEG   xnn = neg_word(xn)            P_DIFF  td = add_sm(xp, xnn)      P_DEC   dd = add_sm(td, OFF)
;   P_BIT   b = dd > 0 (sar_adc's decide, split over three clocks), the code takes the bit; the last decision stops here, the others load
;           the plate's ratio K from the DAC ROM
;   P_MUL   K x VCM as two shifted adds (VCM = 2^23 + 2^22 = 0.75 V: the plate's step is a constant times a ROM constant, so no live operand is
;           multiplied: no DSP slice, no serial multiplier)
;   P_RND   round_back of the product       P_APP   xp and xn take the step, with opposite signs, and the next decision starts
; No clock chains more than one add_sm: the spec's decide() is neg_word and two add_sm in one expression, and it is split here over three clocks
; (a test compares the split with decide). A conversion is 75 clocks from P_SMP to the verdict (a test pins it); no loop depends on data. After
; the verdict the receipt line is sent, then the next conversion runs.
; -
; THE RESTART. As M1b: the button and LOCKED pass M0's two registers; while they say no the request flags `fin` and `hard` are set every clock
; and the next clock puts the machine at conversion 0 and line 0. A finished line sets `fin` alone and the next clock starts the next
; conversion. After conversion 30 the board goes back to conversion 0, so the 31 lines repeat for as long as the capture runs (L counts on).
; -
; THE ROMS (if-chains: `t27b verilog` refuses array indexing; a test compares every word with the spec's own table).
;   rom_vp, rom_vn  q_sm(S_VP[k]), q_sm(S_VN[k]): the held top plates of conversion k, V(VDP) and V(VDN) of the ngspice run at 500 k + 98 ns
;   rom_exp         FIT_CODE[k]: what the spec's fitted converter gives (the board must print it as C)
;   rom_ng          NG_CODE[k]: the code of the ngspice run (printed as N, not judged)
;   rom_k           model_k(UNITS, 1.0, CP_FIT)[2 j + 1], the Vout ratio of plate j (j = 0 is Bit_1): the fitted DAC, 10 words
;   OFF_WORD        q_sm(OFF_FIT_V): the comparator offset, +6.7 mV
; -
; THE RECEIPT. 115200 baud on N15 (divider 868 from 100 MHz), one line per conversion, M0's grammar:
;   T27 SAR K=<2 hex> C=<3 hex> E=<3 hex> N=<3 hex> S=<16 hex> L=<4 hex> PASS
; K the conversion (0 .. 1E), C the board's 11-bit code, E the spec's code for it, N the ngspice code, S the order-sensitive fold of the board's
; codes of this round (K = 0 .. this one), L the lines since the button. PASS when C equals E, else FAIL. N is not judged: 30 of the 31 E equal N
; (conversion 25, K=19 in hex: 1841 against 1842, is the one the spec reports as a miss at 0.133 mV from a threshold). LEDs (active low) as M0: B13
; the line is being sent, C13 FAIL, D14 PASS, D15 a heartbeat. The button T6 resets.
; -
; THE NEGATIVE CONTROL. One literal of rom_k changed: plate j = 0 (Bit_1) with the ratio of 2 units instead of 1, word 16083 to 32166, which is
; one more DAC unit on the LSB plate. The spec's own converter on that table gives the codes FAULT_CODE; 16 of the 31 conversions differ from
; E (FAULT_MASK), and a build with that one literal changed prints FAIL on exactly those lines and PASS on the other 15.
; -
; WHAT A PASS SAYS. This board, running RTL generated from this file, ran the converter of sar_adc.t27 on the 31 held samples and produced, for
; every conversion, the code that spec's fitted model produces (the tests compare the machine with convert_sar on all 31, and the voltage of
; the top plates after every one of the eleven decisions with the spec's own DAC events). By that spec 30 of those 31 codes are the ones the
; ngspice + PSP103 run of the golden deck gave.
; WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY. Nothing about the circuit beyond the spec: the comparator and the top-plate load are two fitted numbers (OFF_FIT_V, CP_FIT),
; fitted on these 31 conversions, so 30 of 31 describes this run and predicts nothing; the switch is the run's, not modelled; the SAR logic is
; a sequence, not gates. Nothing about speed: a conversion takes 75 clocks (0.75 us) and 63 characters of line (5.5 ms), which is not a
; comparison with the 65 minutes of ngspice. Nothing about power, noise, mismatch, another corner or another sample set. The board holds
; ROMs of the samples: it does not sample anything. ASCII only, English only.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module FpgaSarAdc;

use analog::linear;
use analog::sar_cdac;
use analog::sar_adc;
use fpga::rc_filter_ax7203;

pub const KIND : str = "board-cell";
pub const ID : str = "fpga/sar_adc_ax7203";
pub const REFERENCE : str = "specs/analog/sar_adc.t27 (M4e), specs/analog/sar_cdac.t27 (M4a), M1b specs/fpga/analog_cell_ax7203.t27";
pub const BOARD : str = "ALINX AX7203";
pub const PART : str = "xc7a200tfbg484-2";

; --- the converter's numbers, as the board holds them ----------------------------------------------
/// The conversions the board cycles through (sar_adc's N_CONV, as a u8).
pub const CONVS : u8 = 31;
/// The decisions of a conversion (sar_adc's DECISIONS, as a u8), and the index of the last.
pub const DECS : u8 = 11;
pub const DEC_LAST : u8 = 10;
/// The index of the last plate (sar_cdac's PLATES - 1): the first decision moves it.
pub const PLATE_LAST : u8 = 9;
/// q_sm(OFF_FIT_V): +6.7 mV in units of 2^-24 V.
pub const OFF_WORD : u32 = 112407;
/// The clocks from P_SMP to the verdict, as a test measures them: 1 + 10 * 7 + 4.
pub const CONV_CLOCKS : u32 = 75;
/// The order-sensitive fold of the 31 codes of a round (FIT_CODE), the S of the line K = 1E.
pub const ROUND_FOLD : u64 = 0xADF99975C7;

; --- the negative control: one more DAC unit on the LSB plate --------------------------------------
/// The plate and the word of rom_k that the control changes (the right word is 16083), and the 2 units' ratio it is.
pub const FAULT_J : u8 = 0;
pub const FAULT_WORD : u32 = 32166;
/// Bit k set: conversion k prints FAIL with the changed word.
pub const FAULT_MASK : u32 = 687562312;
pub const FAULT_FAILS : u32 = 16;
/// The codes of the spec's converter on the changed table, conversion by conversion.
pub const FAULT_CODE : [31]u32 = [
    1006, 841, 686, 545,
    421, 321, 249, 205,
    194, 214, 266, 349,
    457, 585, 733, 889,
    1053, 1214, 1370, 1513,
    1634, 1734, 1809, 1850,
    1862, 1841, 1789, 1709,
    1601, 1470, 1325
];

; --- the machine --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const P_SMP : u8 = 0;
pub const P_NEG : u8 = 1;
pub const P_DIFF : u8 = 2;
pub const P_DEC : u8 = 3;
pub const P_BIT : u8 = 4;
pub const P_MUL : u8 = 5;
pub const P_RND : u8 = 6;
pub const P_APP : u8 = 7;

; --- facts --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// The conversion after k: the last goes back to the first.
pub fn next_cv(k: u8) -> u8 {
    if (k == CONVS - 1) { return 0; }
    return k + 1;
}

/// Is the word d above zero? A word is never "negative zero" (pack), so this is: some magnitude and no sign bit.
pub fn is_above(d: u32) -> bool {
    return (d & MAG) != 0 and !is_neg(d);
}

/// PASS when the board's code equals the spec's.
pub fn sar_verdict(c: u32, e: u32) -> u8 {
    if (c == e) { return V_PASS; }
    return V_FAIL;
}

